{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>These are the names of the men.</b> It is necessary to know why Scripture repeats this, since it already said ״וְאֵלֶּה שְׁמוֹתָם״ etc.? And it may be explained according to the words of our Sages, of blessed memory (Sotah 34b), who said, and this is their language: Rabbi Yitzḥak said, this matter is handed down to us from our fathers — the spies were called by names reflecting their deeds, etc. Setur son of Mikha'el, because he turned aside (סָתַר) the words of the Holy One, blessed be He, etc. — end of quotation. Now, since Scripture wanted to say ״וַיִּקְרָא מֹשֶׁה לְהוֹשֵׁעַ בִּן נוּן יְהוֹשֻׁעַ״ — that he prayed for him etc. — the speaker will say: what did Moshe see to pray for Yehoshua? For this reason he prefaced by saying <b>וְאֵלֶּה שְׁמוֹת הָאֲנָשִׁים</b> etc., to alert you that from their names Moshe perceived their evil deeds, for which reason it was necessary to pray for Yehoshua — ״וַיִּקְרָא״ etc. And for this reason he juxtaposed the statement ״אֵלֶּה שְׁמוֹת״ etc. to ״וַיִּקְרָא מֹשֶׁה״ etc. And although I wrote above that he sensed their wickedness from the word ״לְךָ,״ that interpretation is not compelling, and the word ״לְךָ״ may be explained in another manner; it was from their names that he inclined and concluded that they would prove wicked in their mission. Further, perhaps he did not affirm that all of them were wicked, but rather their names — since all their names revealed what they were destined to do." "<b>And Moshe called, etc.</b> Our Sages, of blessed memory, said (Sotah 34b) that he prayed for him, and it is necessary to know why he changed his name, for he could have prayed without changing the name. Perhaps it is that he infused power into his name through the addition of the yod, whose numerical value is ten, so that he could stand against the ten spies. Further, so that he would take the merit and good portion of all ten, according to their saying, of blessed memory (Ḥagigah 15a): the worthy one takes his portion and his fellow's portion."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:08:23.686416893Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}